A core in user mode is not interrupted when another core changes its run queue, its turn or its timer.
A thread with time made ready there would wait behind a turn on spare time, or one due later, for that core's next interrupt.

Caught-by: fuzz-smp2
Report: a turn on spare time runs while a thread with time waits
Witness: fuzz-smp2 cores-join-interrupts

diff --git a/kernel/core.c b/kernel/core.c
--- a/kernel/core.c
+++ b/kernel/core.c
@@ -238,7 +238,7 @@ void core_notify(struct core *c)
      * whose timer may be set past the change, or whose run queue or turn changed, which takes the core at once
      * if the turn is on spare time or its request is due before the turn's.
      */
-    if (c != core_self() && (c->turn == NULL || __atomic_load_n(&c->in_user, __ATOMIC_ACQUIRE))) {
+    if (c != core_self() && (c->turn == NULL)) {
         c->interrupt_owed = true;
     }
 #else
